WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.301
Foreign Minister Dymtro

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.069
Kuleba, welcome to the program.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.870
My pleasure.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.340
We're told that there is a consensus

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.708
that Vladimir Putin

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.711
is not ready to engage in

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.948
any serious roundtable negotiations.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.884
Does that match with what you know?

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.686
Well, yes,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.922
When I look at the update

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.924
from the front line,

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.727
I see that whatever Russia says, it's

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.763
not looking for negotiations

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.998
It's not looking for just peace.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.900
They are on the offensive.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.634
They are

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.870
sending missiles and drones

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.072
and our critical energy infrastructure

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.407
and our cities

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.808
is not behave like this

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.710
when you are seeking negotiations

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.611
or when you're trying

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:45.512
to get the upper hand

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.946
in order to have negotiation.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:47.447
Absurd.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.283
You know, this is the he he wants war.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.553
He wants to destroy Ukraine.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.622
And I believe he's obsessed

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.423
with this idea.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.924
In all your deliberations,

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.459
your meetings, here, face to face

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.360
with many of the world

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.661
leaders, including your allies

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.563
who are supporting your defense.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:07.600
Do you feel that you are now out there

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.401
on the road

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.702
to getting what you need

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.205
to maintain a robust

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.274
defense and even maybe an offense?

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.310
When the war began a year ago.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.412
We realized that we need

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.847
certain types of weapons

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.115
to become capable

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.384
of defending our territory,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.953
but also then liberating our territory.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.122
And there are seven types of weapons

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.856
on this list.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.991
I call it the big seven.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:35.161
And in one year, we unlocked

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.763
six out of seven

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.966
was only fighter planes remaining

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:41.868
on the wish list.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.405
A conversation on

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.507
every type of weapon started with a no.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.844
Every single weapon started with or not.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.279
In the end, we got it.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.014
So if you look back at history,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.584
of course, we got

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.787
almost everything that we asked for.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.691
And it's required a huge evolution

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.825
in many capitals,

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.194
including in D.C., in Washington.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:12.665
So if the word of 20, 22 for us

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:16.736
was weapons, the words for 2023 are

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.406
speed, speed of delivery

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.908
and sustainability.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.476
Everything that has been pledged

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.112
has to arrive on time to be relevant.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:27.847
It's important,

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.883
you know, it has to be relevant,

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.185
relevant for the purposes of our victory.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.622
Are you convinced by all the good words

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.789
you hear that

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.992
your allies will stay with you

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:39.893
to the bitter end

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.794
or for however long it takes

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.396
and that there's no peace

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.331
without Ukraine being at the table.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.200
There's no Ukraine in negotiations

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.168
without Ukraine.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:50.403
The mantra, are you sure about that?

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.271
Or do you feel like

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.139
you're being encouraged

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.208
maybe to look for areas of

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.976
a diplomatic possibility

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.048
I don't believe that someone

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.283
of our close

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.551
some of our closest friends

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.452
will negotiate behind our backs.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.988
So I have trust in that

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.057
Even if someone decides to do so,

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.425
I can tell in advance

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.260
I take the opportunity of people

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.461
watching you,

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.264
whatever you negotiate between our backs,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.433
will be rejected by us,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.102
even if you are the closest friend.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.238
I think it's a fair deal

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.808
I think that our closest friends

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.978
will stay by us until we win.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.048
The question is, of course,

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.250
how much time will it take?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.185
We live in democracies.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.887
Governments change. Leaders change.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.556
So this is why it is so important

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.893
to maintain what is bipartisan support

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.196
in the United States or multiple parties

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.631
and so forth here in Germany,

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.967
so that whoever comes to power,

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.635
the support will be there

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.804
And frankly, yes, I have to be cautious.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.871
I have to show some

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.342
rationality and

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.276
say that, of course,

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.578
you can not trust everyone in this world.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:05.979
But I think

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.480
I don't think it's about trust.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.315
I think it's about a group of countries

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.783
who understand

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.353
that victory of Ukraine is not only

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.622
in the best interests of Ukraine,

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.424
but in their own interests. Yes.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.626
And that is what your president said

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.794
when he came here last year

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.230
to say, our fight is your fight as well.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.031
And you need to help us.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:25.798
And he said it again.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:26.799
He portrayed

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:27.533
this struggle

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.535
as David versus Goliath

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.471
and that David had to win.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.406
Question is, what is winning?

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.907
We see what your

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:35.608
your side is

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:38.111
put that we see the ten point plan.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:41.114
Fundamental in that is that Russia

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:41.981
removes itself

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.049
from all the territories

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.917
occupied since 2014

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.020
when I asked NATO's secretary general

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.388
or any other government

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.989
including the United States

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.424
they won't define

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.059
what winning looks like again.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.427
It's up to you.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.596
But one year later,

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.031
what does winning look like?

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.667
Full restoration of Ukraine's

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.934
territorial integrity.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.369
This is the

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.504
the first victory

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.306
that we have to gain on the ground.

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:08.875
Then other victories will follow.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.077
On making Russia compensate,

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.413
on bringing perpetrators to account.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.983
But more broadly speaking,

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.986
we have to answer

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.221
the most important question.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:25.224
What needs to be done to ensure

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.759
lasting peace

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.493
in the region

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.762
and in the whole Euro-Atlantic area?

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.665
And this question has two answers.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.200
First, half of the answer is

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:34.667
that Ukraine

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.703
has to become a member of EU, NATO.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.173
And the second is Russia must change.

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.242
And this is the most intriguing debate

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:46.212
that has to unfold

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.451
what to do with Russia?

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.420
Well, what to do with Russia?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.222
Definitely something

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.490
something needs to be done.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.859
Russia cannot stay as it is now

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.295
because it's full of aggression.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:05.198
It's full of Roman schism.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.533
And I'm not necessarily saying that it's

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.403
something that we outsiders

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.804
have to do with Russia.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:13.673
I think the people of Russia themselves

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.541
have to start thinking

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.143
what needs to be changed

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.245
for their normal life to be brought back

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.448
to their to their daily routine.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.016
It's a complicated issue.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:24.617
There is no

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:25.852
there are no easy answers

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:26.919
at this at this point.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.154
But what I'm trying to say

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:28.821
is that

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:29.922
in the end, lasting

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.724
and enduring peace is possible

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:34.060
when Russia will not be posing a threat.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.962
You have said that

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.063
it's a good deal

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:39.766
what you have with your allies,

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:42.702
but they supply you with the weapons

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.270
so that you do the fighting

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.972
and they don't need to fight.

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:47.607
Do you think that message has got through

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.076
You think they

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:53.079
think Ukraine is

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.281
their existential threat as well?

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.217
Ukraine is Russia is their existence?

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.486
No. I mean, Ukraine is definitely not.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:03.122
There is I mean, a Ukrainian defeat

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.860
It depends on whom you are talking to.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.096
But one way or another, yes,

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.130
they understand it

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.398
because

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.333
whatever the price of supporting

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.535
Ukraine is,

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:17.570
the price of fighting on your own

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:20.606
yourself is will be much higher.

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:23.976
One thing is to send a tank to Ukraine,

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.845
and it may be difficult decision to make,

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.880
but one thing is to send a tank.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.249
Another is to put the young boy

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:31.717
into into the tank

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:34.153
and send him to die for another country.

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:36.789
And I would like to reiterate

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:39.559
once more that we never, never,

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.594
ever asked for foreign boots

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:42.862
on the ground in Ukraine.

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:44.831
And this is why I call it a fair deal.

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:45.431
Unlike

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.399
so many countries

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:48.501
who are calling the United States

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:50.269
to step in

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.370
to come and save them,

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.339
we said we know how to save ourselves

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:55.975
Give us the devil's

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:56.876
sling, so

00:07:56.876 --> 00:07:59.245
to say, to defeat, to defeat Goliath.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:02.315
How long will it take you to win

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.851
It's the most painful question.

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:05.751
I,

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:09.655
I think we should not be asking ourselves

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:10.857
this question.

00:08:10.857 --> 00:08:11.724
I think every day,

00:08:11.724 --> 00:08:13.893
instead of asking ourselves

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.661
how long will it take to win?

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:15.995
We shouldn't

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.029
be asking ourselves,

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:19.966
what else can I do to make Ukraine win?

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:22.201
It completely changes the optics

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:22.869
because if you ask

00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:25.071
the first question, in the end,

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:27.340
you'll get where you get tired.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.174
Right?

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:28.608
Okay.

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:30.977
Silence still goes on.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:33.980
But if you're committed to success,

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.182
it actually motivates you.

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:37.750
It moves you,

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.951
drive, drives, drives you on.

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:40.620
It moves you forward.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.654
And we did.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:42.455
We did succeed.

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.055
In changing

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:46.325
very important optics sometime last year.

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:49.562
Because if you if you see what leaders

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:50.496
were saying

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:51.964
in the beginning of the war,

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.266
they were mostly emphasizing

00:08:53.266 --> 00:08:56.836
that Russia must not prevail in Ukraine.

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:00.273
And we were saying, no, this is wrong

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:01.340
optics

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.242
to get all your policies

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:04.110
and decisions right.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.245
You have to say Ukraine must win.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.180
And now you are hearing more

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.482
and more of that.

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:10.750
These little things,

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.151
they really have an impact on

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.686
what kind of decisions are being made

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.021
and what kind of policies

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:16.422
are being pursued.

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:18.090
So the same here.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.725
Foreign Minister, thank you very much.

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:20.225
Thank you.

